Input: {"question": "In which significant event was Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal involved?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 123, "text": "**HEADLINE:** Terrell's Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal Makes History with Unprecedented Display of Community Consent"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 125, "end": 256, "text": "**TERRELL, TEXAS -** In a remarkable display of unity and cooperation, the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal, located at 200 W."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 257, "end": 411, "text": "College St., has made headlines by becoming the first religious institution in the state to achieve 100% community consent for a major renovation project."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 412, "end": 526, "text": "The historic church, a staple of Terrell's downtown area, has been a hub of community activity for over a century."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 527, "end": 610, "text": "However, as the congregation grew, so did the need for expansion and modernization."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 611, "end": 789, "text": "In response, the church leadership proposed a comprehensive renovation plan, which included the addition of new facilities, improved accessibility, and energy-efficient upgrades."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 790, "end": 962, "text": "What sets this project apart is the church's commitment to obtaining explicit consent from every single member of the community, a feat that has never been achieved before."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 963, "end": 980, "text": "According to Rev."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 981, "end": 1128, "text": "Emily Wilson, Rector of the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal, \"We wanted to ensure that every voice was heard and every concern was addressed."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1129, "end": 1257, "text": "We believe that this project belongs to the entire community, and we wanted to make sure everyone felt invested in its success.\""}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1258, "end": 1388, "text": "The consent process, which spanned several months, involved a series of town hall meetings, surveys, and one-on-one consultations."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1389, "end": 1561, "text": "Church members and local residents were encouraged to share their thoughts, concerns, and suggestions, which were carefully documented and incorporated into the final plan."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1562, "end": 1704, "text": "\"I was blown away by the level of engagement and enthusiasm from the community,\" said Karen Thompson, a long-time church member and volunteer."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1705, "end": 1815, "text": "\"It was amazing to see people from all walks of life come together to shape the future of our beloved church.\""}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1816, "end": 1954, "text": "The data speaks for itself: out of a total of 1,200 community members surveyed, 100% provided explicit consent for the renovation project."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1955, "end": 2090, "text": "This unprecedented level of agreement is a testament to the church's dedication to transparency, inclusivity, and community engagement."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2091, "end": 2268, "text": "The renovation project, which is expected to be completed within the next 18 months, will not only enhance the church's facilities but also provide a boost to the local economy."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2269, "end": 2429, "text": "According to a study by the Terrell Chamber of Commerce, the project is expected to generate over $1 million in economic activity and create dozens of new jobs."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2430, "end": 2614, "text": "As the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal embarks on this exciting new chapter, its commitment to community consent serves as a beacon of hope and cooperation for the entire region."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2615, "end": 2622, "text": "As Rev."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 83, "text": "Title: The Pillar of Faith: Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal's Enduring Legacy"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 85, "end": 219, "text": "In the heart of Terrell, Texas, a beacon of hope and spirituality stands tall, a testament to the power of community and perseverance."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 220, "end": 281, "text": "The Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal, situated at 200 W."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 282, "end": 355, "text": "College St., has been a cornerstone of the city's fabric for generations."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 356, "end": 470, "text": "Behind its elegant façade lies a rich history, woven from the threads of faith, dedication, and economic activity."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 471, "end": 610, "text": "This narrative delves into the significant event of construction that shaped the church's identity and cemented its place in the community."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 611, "end": 773, "text": "The year was 1885, and Terrell was a burgeoning town, its population swelling with settlers drawn to the area's fertile soil and promising economic opportunities."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 774, "end": 920, "text": "As the town grew, so did the need for a spiritual hub, a place where residents could come together to worship, find solace, and forge connections."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 921, "end": 1006, "text": "It was against this backdrop that the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal was born."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1007, "end": 1126, "text": "The construction of the church was a monumental undertaking, one that required the collective efforts of the community."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1127, "end": 1224, "text": "Parishioners, local businessmen, and skilled craftsmen joined forces to bring the vision to life."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1225, "end": 1369, "text": "The project was a significant economic activity, injecting life into the local economy and creating jobs for laborers, carpenters, and artisans."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1370, "end": 1492, "text": "As the church began to take shape, it became a symbol of hope and progress, a beacon of light in a rapidly changing world."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1493, "end": 1561, "text": "The church's design was a masterclass in elegance and functionality."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1562, "end": 1720, "text": "The Gothic Revival style, popular during the late 19th century, was chosen for its soaring vertical lines, pointed arches, and stunning stained-glass windows."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1721, "end": 1845, "text": "The building's façade, constructed from locally sourced limestone, was a testament to the region's rich geological heritage."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1846, "end": 2020, "text": "The attention to detail was meticulous, from the intricately carved wooden pews to the majestic bell tower, which would soon become a beloved landmark in the Terrell skyline."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2021, "end": 2150, "text": "As the construction progressed, the church became a hub of activity, with townspeople gathering to watch the building take shape."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2151, "end": 2320, "text": "The sound of hammers ringing out, the smell of freshly cut wood, and the sight of workers hauling heavy stones into place created a sense of excitement and anticipation."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2321, "end": 2485, "text": "The church was more than just a building; it was a symbol of community, a testament to the power of collective effort, and a beacon of hope for generations to come."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal", "scope": "significant event", "claim": "The Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal was involved in the significant event of construction that shaped its identity.", "answer": "construction", "quote": "This narrative delves into the significant event of construction that shaped the church's identity and cemented its place in the community. The year was 1885, and Terrell was a burgeoning town, its population swelling with settlers drawn to the area's fertile soil and promising economic opportunities. As the town grew, so did the need for a spiritual hub, a place where residents could come together to worship, find solace, and forge connections. It was against this backdrop that the Church of the Good Shepherd Episcopal was born. The construction of the church was a monumental undertaking, one that required the collective efforts of the community.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["unprecedented display of community consent for a major renovation project", "construction", "major renovation project", "town hall meetings", "surveys", "one-on-one consultations"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "unprecedented display of community consent for a major renovation project", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "construction", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "major renovation project", "origin": "coverage_addition"}, {"candidate_id": "R3", "answer": "town hall meetings", "origin": "coverage_addition"}, {"candidate_id": "R4", "answer": "surveys", "origin": "coverage_addition"}, {"candidate_id": "R5", "answer": "one-on-one consultations", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}
